title: 'statement-store: bound inbound statement decode by memory'

doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    Inbound statement notifications are now decoded under a memory budget, so a peer can't turn a
    small message into a large allocation before the rate limiter runs. A batch that exceeds the
    budget is dropped and the peer disconnected; other decode failures stay a bad-message report.

crates:
- name: sc-network-statement
  bump: minor
